claim: "Petals on the Wind is a 2014 Lifetime movie sequel of the film which starred The Leftovers actress Kiernan Brennan Shipka."
evidences (the complete set of findings collected so far, oldest first):
[
 {
  "finding": {
   "question": "Is Petals on the Wind a 2014 Lifetime movie sequel of a film?",
   "answer": "Yes, Petals on the Wind is a 2014 Lifetime movie sequel to the 2014 adaptation Flowers in the Attic.",
   "source": "Petals on the Wind (film) https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Petals_on_the_Wind_(film)",
   "excerpt": "Petals on the Wind is a 2014 Lifetime movie sequel to the 2014 adaptation Flowers in the Attic, starring Heather Graham, Rose McIver, Wyatt Nash, Bailey Buntain and Ellen Burstyn.",
   "stance": "SUPPORTS"
  },
  "passage": "Title: Petals on the Wind\nURL: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Petals_on_the_Wind\nExcerpt: Petals on the Wind is a novel written by V. C. Andrews in 1980. It is the second book in the Dollanganger series. The timeline takes place from the siblings' successful escape in November 1960 to the fall of 1975.  The book, like the others in the series, was a number one best-seller in North America in the early 1980s. In 2014, it was adapted into a Lifetime original movie.\n\nTitle: Flowers in the Attic (2014 film)\nURL: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flowers_in_the_Attic_(2014_film)\nExcerpt: Flowers in the Attic is a 2014 Lifetime psychological thriller drama movie directed by Deborah Chow. It is the second adaptation of V. C. Andrews’ 1979 novel of the same name.\nA sequel, Petals on the Wind, based on the novel of the same name, premiered on May 26, 2014, on Lifetime. The network announced the developing of the following books in the series, If There Be Thorns and Seeds of Yesterday, which both aired in 2015.\n\nTitle: Wyatt Nash\nURL: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wyatt_Nash\nExcerpt: Matthew Wyatt Elrod (born October 2, 1988), better known as Wyatt Nash, is an American television personality and actor.\nUnder his birth name, he was a contestant on the 22nd season of the American competitive reality television series Survivor where he placed seventh. Following his appearance on Survivor: Redemption Island, he chose to adopt the name Wyatt Nash (his middle name plus Nash for his birth city, Nashville) as his stage name.\nNash has appeared as Nigel Wright on the ABC Family series Pretty Little Liars and the Lifetime television adaptation of V. C. Andrews's Petals on the Wind. He portrayed the character of Charles Smith on Riverdale.\n\nTitle: Petals on the Wind (film)\nURL: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Petals_on_the_Wind_(film)\nExcerpt: Petals on the Wind is a 2014 Lifetime movie sequel to the 2014 adaptation Flowers in the Attic, starring Heather Graham, Rose McIver, Wyatt Nash, Bailey Buntain and Ellen Burstyn. It is based on V. C. Andrews' 1980 novel of the same name, the second novel on the Dollanganger series. The film follows the surviving Dollanganger children—Cathy, Chris and Carrie—ten years after escaping the attic. Despite attempting to move on with their lives, after multiple failed attempts and tragedies occur, Cathy decides it is time to take revenge on her mother.\nLifetime first announced the film shortly before Flowers in the Attic was released. The network announced on the premiere of the movie the developing of the following books of the Dollanganger series, If There Be Thorns and Seeds of Yesterday, both of which aired in 2015.\nThe film received a positive response from critics.\n\nTitle: If There Be Thorns (film)\nURL: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/If_There_Be_Thorns_(film)\nExcerpt: If There Be Thorns is a 2015 television film based on the best-selling 1981 novel of the same name. It premiered on April 5, 2015, and was produced by Lifetime. Seeds of Yesterday is the sequel film based on the novel of the same name."
 },
 {
  "finding": {
   "question": "Did Kiernan Brennan Shipka, known for The Leftovers, star in Petals on the Wind?",
   "answer": "INSUFFICIENT",
   "source": "",
   "excerpt": "",
   "stance": "INSUFFICIENT"
  },
  "passage": ""
 }
]

